# Sum of Positive

```javascript
function positiveSum(arr) {
  return arr.reduce((total, n) => (n > 0 ? total + n : total), 0);
}
```

A single left-to-right pass, adding each element only when it is positive. Seeding `reduce` with `0` also gives the right answer for an empty array and for an array with no positive values, both of which the notes call out.

O(n) time, O(1) extra space.

# Highest and Lowest

```javascript
function highAndLow(numbers){
  const values = numbers.split(' ').map(Number);
  return `${Math.max(...values)} ${Math.min(...values)}`;
}
```

Split on the single space the notes guarantee, convert to numbers, then take both extremes in one pass each. The result is a string of the highest and lowest separated by a space, which is what the sample tests assert.

O(n) time, O(n) space for the parsed values.

