# Two Sum

```python
class Solution:
    def twoSum(self, nums: List[int], target: int) -> List[int]:
        seen = {}
        for index, value in enumerate(nums):
            complement = target - value
            if complement in seen:
                return [seen[complement], index]
            seen[value] = index
        return []
```

A single pass with a map from value to index, as asked out loud: for each element the complement is looked up before the element itself is stored, so an index is never paired with itself. The guarantee of exactly one answer means the first hit can be returned immediately.

O(n) time, O(n) space.
